cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  What survives? Semantic eligibility, distribution shift and metric
  interpretation in external validation of ADMET predictors
message: >-
  If you use this analysis, the frozen result artefacts or the semantic
  eligibility protocol, please cite this preprint.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Roktim
    given-names: Rahul Reza
    # Supply before release; see USER_INPUT_REQUIRED.md
    affiliation: "Department of Pharmacy, Daffodil International University, Dhaka, Bangladesh"
    orcid: "0009-0003-6518-0495"
    email: "roktim2311091058@diu.edu.bd"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, frozen result artefacts, figures and manuscript for a
  pre-specified semantic eligibility screen applied to twelve candidate
  external dataset-to-model-output pairings for ADMET-AI 2.0.1, together with
  the external performance, baseline comparison, label-distribution shift and
  prediction-range compression analyses for the three accepted pairings.
keywords:
  - ADMET
  - external validation
  - distribution shift
  - model calibration
  - cheminformatics
  - reproducibility
version: 1.0.0-preprint
license: MIT
